From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:11:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: apple: atc: set a DisplayPort mode up again after a deep
 sleep

A T8140 PHY carrying DisplayPort doesn't sleep in place: its USB
controller stops for the sleep instead. The sleep's commit then lowers
ATC0_COMMON itself, behind the power domain's back, so the lanes, the
tunables and the AUX channel are gone at the wake while the driver still
tracks the DP mode the Type-C mux asked for. Nothing set them up again,
so an external display that stayed attached through the sleep could
never train its link.

After a sleep that reached its commit, mark such a PHY's domain as having
been off, so that atcphy_resume() brings the tracked mode back through
atcphy_restore_after_pd_off(), before the display controller resumes and
connects the link anew. A sleep in place keeps its own restore, and a
refused sleep left the block powered.

Signed-off-by: Diljit Singh <hey@djdev.me>
---
 drivers/phy/apple/atc.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
index 3eef1ec203..8ac28884b0 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
@@ -6785,14 +6785,32 @@ static int atcphy_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * A PHY in a DisplayPort mode doesn't sleep in place, and a sleep that reached its commit
+ * lowered ATC0_COMMON under it, behind its power domain's back: the lanes and the AUX
+ * channel went. Have atcphy_resume() set the tracked mode up again, before the display
+ * controller connects the link anew.
+ */
+static void atcphy_sleep_lost_dp(struct apple_atcphy *atcphy)
+{
+	if (!atcphy->hw->has_t8140_dp || !atcphy->hw->restore_after_pd_off ||
+	    !pm_resume_via_firmware() || !atcphy_modes[atcphy->mode].enable_dp_aux)
+		return;
+	WRITE_ONCE(atcphy->pd_was_off, true);
+	dev_dbg(atcphy->dev, "DisplayPort mode %d lost in the sleep: setting it up again\n",
+		atcphy->mode);
+}
+
 static int atcphy_resume_noirq(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct apple_atcphy *atcphy = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	guard(mutex)(&atcphy->lock);
-	if (!atcphy->hibernated)
+	if (!atcphy->hibernated) {
+		atcphy_sleep_lost_dp(atcphy);
 		return 0;
+	}
 	apple_sleep_usb_set_asleep(false);
 
 	atcphy_usb2_sleep_exit(atcphy);
